## 🎯 Goal Setting

- [ ] Schedule an individual goal-setting session to define and track your goals with your mentor, updating them in your **agenda repository**.

**✅ Steps**
- [ ] Develop your **personal agenda** with key tasks and learning objectives
- [ ] Set **mid-term** goals (per semester), and work on them in weekly iterations
- [ ] Align with team priorities and update goals regularly
- [ ] Explore internal and external **learning opportunities** (workshops, conferences, online courses)

**🗓 Regular Check-ins**
- **Weekly/Biweekly**: 1:1 mentor meeting
- **Semester**: Goal review & adjustments

**Take ownership, ask for support, and grow with the team! 🚀**

---

## 💻 Your Workplace

Your workspace setup depends on your role:

- **Student assistants** typically work on their own machines.
- **PhD students** can request a **laptop** through our **team assistant**.
- Work can be done **remotely**, in the **library**, or at a **workspace of your choice**.

**✅ IT Setup**
- [ ] Set up your **computer, email, and network accounts**
- [ ] Ask your supervisor to create your [e-mail account](https://www.uni-bamberg.de/its/dienstleistungen/mail/wlv/exchange/), using the [GitHub mention](https://github.blog/news-insights/mention-somebody-they-re-notified/) feature (IAM-Portal: Antrag auf ein persönliches Nutzerkonto/E-Mail-Konto). Forward e-mails from stud to uni-mail (Posteingangs- und Aufräumregeln).
- [ ] Develop a short biography and ask (mention) our **team assistant** to add you to the team page on our [website](https://www.uni-bamberg.de/digital-work/team/) (together with a photo)

> [!NOTE]
> There is an external-HDD setup for student assistants.

**🌐 GitHub**
- [ ] Navigate to the [digital-work-lab team](https://github.com/orgs/digital-work-lab/teams/digital-work-team) and request to join.
- [ ] Update your **GitHub account**: add `Otto-Friedrich-Universität Bamberg` as your organization, upload a photo or avatar, and add yourself to the [team page](https://digital-work-lab.github.io/handbook/docs/01.team.html) (create an [ORCiD](https://orcid.org/register) account)
- [ ] Familiarize yourself with our [GitHub repositories](https://digital-work-lab.github.io/handbook/docs/10-lab/18_resources/18.12.repositories.html) and workflows. Request access to relevant **repositories** and bookmark important links.

**🎓 Teaching**
- [ ] Register for relevant VC courses

**📌 Research & Work Hub**
- [ ] Explore our [work_hub](https://github.com/digital-work-lab/work_hub) for shared knowledge management
- [ ] PhD students: sign and submit [ethics statement](https://github.com/digital-work-lab/handbook/blob/b88fafe6071d3e9168a1e185bbc91d8cefd6ef1e/assets/docs/1_OFU_25_Empfangsbest%C3%A4tigung_Sicherung_GWP_Praxis_01.03.24.pdf)

**📢 Announcements**
- [ ] [Aktuelle Informationen der Fachschaft WIAI](https://vc.uni-bamberg.de/user/view.php?id=1157&course=284)
- [ ] [AIS-Mailing list](https://aisnet.org/page/AISWorldListserve)

**Make sure your setup is complete before diving into your first tasks! 🛠️**

